// Extra US 1.0 symbols found for the randomizer, merged with spm-headers' lst at build time.
// relF entries are module,section,offset: section 1 = file offset - 0xdc, section 5 = file offset - 0xaf300
// (offsets in the decompressed relF.rel; see DESIGN.md for how each was found)

// main.dol
8011EFD0:guideGetWork
800E0E74:evt_door_select_entry
800E1078:evt_door_select_set
803D8468:door_enter_evt
// In the "can the current character use their ability" check (0x80147A08): the
// bl evtGetValue(GSW(0)) whose result blocks Mario's flip when 0 < value < 16
80147AB4:mario_flip_story_check
// File select (seq_load_sub draw, per save r17, heart index r23): lwz r3, 0x148(r17) (the save's
// GSW 0); lwz r0, 0(r21) (threshold table 0x803E9108: 4, 53, 95, 125, 173, 220, 286, 353);
// cmplw r3, r0; blt (skip drawing heart r23)
8017EF8C:filesel_heart_check
// marioStatusApplyStatuses(status, lv), as marioTakeDamage calls it. spm-headers' us0 lst lists that
// name at 804CEA28 first (the pouch, not code) and only later at the real address, and the first wins
80154448:mario_status_apply
// Key item menu (pluswinKeyItemMain), using the selected key item: cmplwi r0, 0x24 (Floro Sprout);
// bne +0x48 (to the Return Pipe's check at +0x4c). The Floro Sprout's path starts at +8 and runs its
// script with bl evtEntryType at +0x2c (r3 = script, r4-r6 = 0), then stores the entry for the menu
80188374:keyitem_menu_use_check
// Key item menu drawing, per item (r25 = item id): cmpwi r25, 0x32; bne normal; then the Return
// Pipe's enable bytes decide whether its icon / name is drawn greyed out
80188B1C:keyitem_icon_pipe_check
80188C18:keyitem_name_pipe_check
// Pause menu (pluswinOpen 0x801851E8, pluswinMain 0x80185A58; EU0 names, US addresses are EU0 - 0xCEC
// for these). The Maps button (button 7, texture 7) is only created, and the cursor only stops on it,
// if any of the 12 map bits in the pouch (+0x30C) is set, which the US game never does: both places
// call that count (bl 0x8014F394), one in pluswinOpen's button loop, one in the cursor check
// pluswinCheckHaveMaps (0x801851B4, nav table 0x803E9F50). Selecting it plays SFX_SYS_MENU_DESIDE1,
// calls pluswinMapsWinOpen and sets the menu to state 50, which waits until the window in
// submenuEntryIds[0] is deleted, then goes back to the buttons
80185308:pluswin_open_maps_count
801851C0:pluswin_check_maps_count
801907CC:pluswinMapsWinOpen
// spsndBGMOn_f_d(flags, name, fadeMsec): every song starts here (spsndBGMOn and the alternate entry
// branch to it). It looks the name up in spsbgmlist (BgmEntry[150], allocated and filled at startup)
80239EDC:spsndBGMOn_f_d
// The 3 music players (BgmPlayer, 0x28 each): bgmEntry, then the nw4r sound handle (null once the
// sound has ended)
804EFFD8:spsndBgmPlayers
// (player, fadeMsec): brings a music player's volume back up after it was turned down (0x8023A9F4,
// (player, volume, fadeMsec)); the item window does this to players 0 and 1 when it stops player 2's
// jingle (itemCollectPouchItem area, 0x8007AC74)
8023AAE8:bgm_volume_restore
// Sound effects: every effect starts in __spsndSFXOn, which bsearches spssfxlist (SfxEntry[count],
// 0x14 each, sorted by name: name, u16 sound archive index, ...; filled at startup from
// sound/wiimario_snd.dat) with the count at 0x804F0A4A. The 32 effect players (0x3C each, at
// 0x804F0060) point at their SfxEntry; these two look a name up among them (EU0 spsndSFX_chkName and
// spsndSFX_getIdPlayingName, US = EU0 - 0x25FC)
8056DA3C:spssfxlist
804F0A4A:spsnd_sfx_count
802394FC:sfx_check_name
802395DC:sfx_id_playing_name
// Called only by Fleep's join scene (sp2_01), right after the join (names are guesses): with 1, the
// first sets MarioWork flag 0x00200000 and gives an object callback 0x8012CA18, mode 6; the second
// changes that object's mode. Tippi's pointer crashes afterwards if Mario has no Fleep
// Not in spm-headers' lst; called by evt_pouch_set_pixl_selected
8014E914:pouchSetPixlSelected
800F2838:evt_fleep_mode_on
800F2878:evt_fleep_mode_set

// The title screen's work (SeqTitleWork in spm-headers' seq_title.h, allocated by seq_titleInit):
// seq_titleMain (0x8017A5B8) reads the pointer with lwz -0x7E50(r13), r13 = 0x80574F20. animNum 0 is
// the opening animation (title_Start, 121 frames: the logo drops in and settles by frame 40), 1 the
// loop (title_Loop, 860 frames: the logo sways at frames 230-380 and 630-780). seq_titleMain enters
// the title's drawing on CAM_ID_2D, render mode 4, z 1000 (in mode 4, smaller z is drawn later)
8056D0D0:seq_title_wp
// The title's display callback (0x8017AC14) animates the layout, then works out where each pane goes
// (CalculateMtx) and draws it, all in one call. The animate call: lwz r12, 0x2c(vtable); bctrl, with
// r3 = the layout, r4 = 0. Layout: root pane at +0x10. Panes: FindPaneByName at vtable +0x3C (as
// seqTitleInitLayout uses it), translation (x, y, z) at +0x2C
8017AD10:title_layout_animate_call

// A Pixl's work (0xD0 bytes) by its id, or 0 if there's none (only searches while the Pixl list is on)
8011DEB0:fairy_work_by_id
// In Mario's flip: if he has a Pixl id (mario+0x1484), it looks up that Pixl (bl fairy_work_by_id) and
// sets bit 2 of its first halfword, without checking that the Pixl is there
80147934:flip_pixl_lookup_call

// In Tippi's pointer code: "cmpwi r3, 12; blt off" on the story value: no pointing while it's 1-11
// (vanilla: before her pointing tutorial at the start of 1-1)
802421E4:tippi_pointer_story_check

// Mario's climbing (motion 13) reads the stick each frame and adds its direction (1 unit at full tilt)
// to his climbing move: vertical at mario+0x138, sideways at mario+0x134, which the movement code then
// applies. These are those adds: in 2D, up and down twice and sideways once; in 3D, up and down twice
8011A6F4:climb_2d_vertical_add_1
8011A704:climb_2d_vertical_add_2
8011A71C:climb_2d_sideways_add
8011AB44:climb_3d_vertical_add_1
8011AB54:climb_3d_vertical_add_2

